{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error. The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item. For source identities the application can supply independently, implement `source_address` to recover the project-relative outline address from the domain identity. Other identities return `None`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`. Each obligation maps to a marked test with an assertion that enforces it.\n\n**Mapping a supported address to `NodeData` and interning it as a `NodeId`**\n- `agent_node_addresses_round_trip_and_reject_inconsistent_identities_before_reads` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` reads `parser.rs#impl[Parser]` by path/location and by data.\n- It asserts that the child node ids equal `intern_node(\"parser.rs#impl[Parser]/fn[parse]\")`. That shows the `Project::source_node` result was interned in the domain cache.\n- It also asserts that the recorded dependencies match the interned nodes.\n- `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` checks that the `TestDomain::source_node` data (`TestNode` ids 7–10) comes back as interned dependencies. It also asserts that `list_sources` entries carry integer node ids and `data`.\n\n**Unsupported or invalid address returns an error**\n- `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` passes two addresses: an unknown path and an unknown selector.\n- Both make the test domain's `source_node` fail. The test asserts the \"unsupported source item\" error, that no dependencies are recorded, and that no reads happen.\n- The read_node test also rejects an invalid path or location such as `absent.rs` or `fn[absent]`. It checks that the domain's `reads` count is unchanged.\n\n**Cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item**\n- `TestDomain` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` does not override `source_address`, so it uses the default, which returns `None`.\n- In `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions`, step 14 calls `read_node` with only the `node` id of a search hit (`unused.txt`, `TestNode` 10). The domain cannot recover that address itself.\n- The test then asserts a dependency on node 10 with the outline fingerprint of the file. That can only happen if the cache kept the address from mapping (`ValidationCache::intern_source`).\n- This discriminates retention from the `source_address` fallback. The `Project` test domain in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` could recover addresses either way, so this test is what covers retention.\n\n**`source_address` recovers the address for identities the application can supply, and returns `None` for others**\n- `habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds` in `src/sdk.rs` asserts the round trip `domain.source_address(&domain.source_node(&method).unwrap()) == Some(method)` for a project-relative item.\n- The same test asserts `source_address == None` for every other node kind: requirement, reference set, selection, definition, a `Source` node with a non-`repo` scheme, and site review.\n- The default `None` implementation is exercised through `TestDomain`, as described above.\n\n**`public_exports_match_the_appendix`** in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs` covers the trait signature shape. The remaining obligations are covered by the behavioural tests above.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behaviour that these tests would accept. Dropping the cached address, interning without mapping, accepting an unsupported address, or returning `Some` for a foreign identity would each fail at least one assertion above.",
  "references": "1d29a32082b25d649b6110366e39b9fc87deb5e567f66edeb4008297385b5324",
